From b641763a4f5fdb0d53e69bc17fe29b339a8646b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:20:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 35/38] WIP: ASoC: codecs: add a Maxim MAX98506 speaker
 amplifier driver

The MAX98506 is a mono class-D amplifier with a boost converter on I2S,
the loudspeaker amplifier of the Galaxy S8+. Register values follow
the vendor driver without its Maxim DSM speaker protection: slave,
clocked from BCLK (32 per frame), moderate gain and the limiter on.
The amplifier is enabled through DAPM.

Not working yet: with the registers equal to the vendor kernel's while
it plays (all of 0x00-0x3f), the speaker stays silent on mainline.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
---
 sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig    |   6 +
 sound/soc/codecs/Makefile   |   2 +
 sound/soc/codecs/max98506.c | 292 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 300 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/codecs/max98506.c

